    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-11-21-000001",
        "note": "PALOMAR-2026-11-21-000001 compares only Corollary 2. It identifies the even bases with exactly one cycle and gives that cycle's length. Theorem 1 classifies every nonconstant cycle in every even base. It identifies all lifts from odd cores with their original periods, classifies the additional cycles and their exact periods, and counts the cycles of each length in every power of two. This includes bases with more than one cycle, for example base 4 with one fixed point and a 2-cycle. Both entries use the same development. Theorem 1 was already proved there and this entry presents its first direct comparison for the digit-sorting map.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/galyavin/kaprekar-dynamics (cycles-even-bases/ancillary/lean)",
        "note": "The substantive Lean development of the paper (Theorem 1 and Corollary 2 for the development's step map on four-slot digit words), by the same author. SolutionTheorem1 imports a port of that development included in this repository and reuses the original Solution's proof relating its step map to the Challenge definition. The port uses Lean's module system and Lean 4.35.0-rc2.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
